{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GTUN3iHrmgFc7u9nNtLmse","type":"tool_result","content":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\tf25ed34b9cd1960b957fc55a\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tAditya Kousik (Jira)\ndate:\t2026-03-31T20:40:00Z\nsubject:\t[jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20384) Per-Record Context Processing for Kafka Consumers\nthread:\tJIRA.13646857.1774989545000@Atlassian.JIRA\nin-reply-to:\tJIRA.13646857.1774989545000@Atlassian.JIRA\n\nAditya Kousik created KAFKA-20384:\n-------------------------------------\n\n             Summary: Per-Record Context Processing for Kafka Consumers\n                 Key: KAFKA-20384\n                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20384\n             Project: Kafka\n          Issue Type: Improvement\n          Components: clients, consumer\n            Reporter: Aditya Kousik\n\n\n ConsumerInterceptor operates at batch level. There is no client-level hook for per-record processing lifecycle (span creation, MDC, context propagation). Frameworks and instrumentation libraries have\n   independently built workarounds. This KIP adds ConsumerRecordContextProcessor to fill that gap. See KIP-1305.\n\n\n\n--\nThis message was sent by Atlassian Jira\n(v8.20.10#820010)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae1b786b-5797-4d1e-a99f-257e8165261c","uuid":"9d8d6d18-4148-4ee7-a658-bca2fa12e53b","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:45:15.626Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\tf25ed34b9cd1960b957fc55a\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tAditya Kousik (Jira)\ndate:\t2026-03-31T20:40:00Z\nsubject:\t[jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20384) Per-Record Context Processing for Kafka Consumers\nthread:\tJIRA.13646857.1774989545000@Atlassian.JIRA\nin-reply-to:\tJIRA.13646857.1774989545000@Atlassian.JIRA\n\nAditya Kousik created KAFKA-20384:\n-------------------------------------\n\n             Summary: Per-Record Context Processing for Kafka Consumers\n                 Key: KAFKA-20384\n                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20384\n             Project: Kafka\n          Issue Type: Improvement\n          Components: clients, consumer\n            Reporter: Aditya Kousik\n\n\n ConsumerInterceptor operates at batch level. There is no client-level hook for per-record processing lifecycle (span creation, MDC, context propagation). Frameworks and instrumentation libraries have\n   independently built workarounds. This KIP adds ConsumerRecordContextProcessor to fill that gap. See KIP-1305.\n\n\n\n--\nThis message was sent by Atlassian Jira\n(v8.20.10#820010)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
